# Security allowlist — read by crates/marion-testsupport/tests/three_axis (run: scripts/three-axis.sh).
#
# Format: `path:item  one-line reason`. A finding not listed here fails the check; an entry nothing
# matches fails it too, so a fix deletes its line. Only VERIFIED-SAFE cases belong here, each
# saying why — plus the `untracked` findings below, listed so the check can gate new code today
# while they are fixed; those are real and are the first to remove.

# --- untracked: secret-bearing structs that derive Debug (a `{:?}` anywhere prints the secret) ---
crates/marion-harness/src/adapter.rs:LaunchSpec  untracked: `api_key: Option<String>` (the operator's endpoint key) under derive(Debug)
crates/marion-harness/src/spec.rs:Fields  untracked: `api_key` string under derive(Debug)
crates/marion-harness/src/cline.rs:ProviderSpec  untracked: `api_key` string under derive(Debug)
crates/marion-harness/src/opencode.rs:ConfigSpec  untracked: `api_key` string under derive(Debug)
crates/marion-harness/src/adapter.rs:SpawnCtx  untracked: per-node bridge `node_token` under derive(Debug)
crates/marion-harness/src/mcp_bridge.rs:BridgeEnv  untracked: per-node bridge `node_token` under derive(Debug)
crates/marion-core/src/proto/params.rs:SpawnCaller  untracked: per-node bridge `node_token` under derive(Debug)
crates/marion-supervisor/src/root.rs:RootNode  untracked: per-run bearer `token` under derive(Debug) (canned endpoint only, still a capability)

# --- verified safe --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
crates/marion-harness/src/adapter.rs:AcpAdapter::config_files  safe: `api_key` is a field init inside the opencode config document, written 0600 by run::write_config_documents
crates/marion-harness/src/adapter.rs:GooseAdapter::fields  safe: `token` is a whitespace-split argv word in an error message, not a credential
crates/marion-supervisor/src/credentials.rs:Keychain::put  safe: the exposed key is formatted into the `security -i` command line sent on stdin, never argv or a log
crates/marion-supervisor/src/root.rs:record_the_roots_change  safe: writes root-change.json (file counts only, no credential); root.rs is marked only because it asks for config_files
crates/marion-supervisor/src/run.rs:persist_then_cap  safe: writes the task contract, which carries credential ids never keys; run.rs's key-bearing docs go through the 0600 write_config_documents
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/endpoint_matrix.rs:a_provider_with_no_stored_key_is_refused_by_name_with_the_login_command  safe: "marion login …" is the expected refusal text, never run
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/login.rs:a_custom_provider_is_added_listed_and_can_hold_a_key  safe: marion's own `marion login` against a scratch HOME/XDG and the file store with a fixture key; no vendor login
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/login.rs:a_key_piped_with_stdin_is_stored_in_the_file_backend_and_never_printed  safe: marion's own `marion login` against a scratch HOME/XDG and the file store with a fixture key; no vendor login
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/login.rs:a_repositorys_own_providers_toml_is_never_read  safe: marion's own `marion login` against a scratch HOME/XDG and the file store with a fixture key; no vendor login
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/login.rs:an_unknown_provider_is_refused_by_name_with_the_command_to_define_it  safe: marion's own `marion login` against a scratch HOME/XDG and the file store with a fixture key; no vendor login
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/login.rs:from_env_imports_the_providers_own_variable_with_explicit_consent  safe: marion's own `marion login` against a scratch HOME/XDG and the file store with a fixture key; no vendor login
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/login.rs:list_shows_every_provider_and_which_are_stored_but_never_the_key  safe: marion's own `marion login` against a scratch HOME/XDG and the file store with a fixture key; no vendor login
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/login.rs:several_labelled_keys_for_one_provider_are_stored_listed_and_removed_one_by_one  safe: marion's own `marion login` against a scratch HOME/XDG and the file store with a fixture key; no vendor login
crates/marion-supervisor/tests/login.rs:without_a_terminal_and_without_a_flag_login_refuses_and_waits_for_nothing  safe: marion's own `marion login` refusing without a terminal; nothing is stored or started

# --- verified safe: login-p3 (2026-09-27) ---
crates/marion-core/src/contract.rs:CredentialFailover  from/to are credential ids (`provider:label`), never keys; the contract records which credential ran, by id
crates/marion-supervisor/src/provider_check.rs:CredentialRow  `id` is a credential id (`provider:label`); the row never holds the key, which goes to curl on stdin only
crates/marion-harness/src/spec.rs:KeyRecipe  `note` is the row's measurement prose; the recipe names header spellings, never a key
crates/marion-harness/src/adapter.rs:render_row  formats the header's *name* ("Authorization: Bearer" / "x-api-key") into a refusal; no key is in scope
crates/marion-supervisor/src/bin/marion.rs:tests::the_usage_text_names_login_and_logout  asserts the help text names `marion login --list`; runs nothing

# --- verified safe: profiles (2026-09-27) ---
crates/marion-harness/src/profile.rs:tests::CARRIER  a fixture carrier's `login_hint`, the words `marion profile add` prints for the operator; nothing runs it
